Subject: FTL: Traversable Wormholes 1 of 1

I think I was the first to bring up the issue of intelligence
being normally distributed in time on this list, but the idea
is not original with me.  It may have come from Casti or Dyson
in one of their books.  What I remember of the discussions
goes like this:
]

You can break down our position in history into two classes:
"We're Number One" and "We're Number Two".  In the first case,
you assume that we are the first intelligent civilization.  If
you make an assumption about the variability of how fast intelligence
evolves, and how many places life is evolving, you can estimate
how long it should be between the first and second intelligent
species in a normal distribution.  

I then guessed what I consider reasonable values, and you typically
get millions of years between #1 and #2.  Thus either there is
no other civilization close to intelligence (if we are #1), or
there is a civilization millions of years ahead of us, by which time
they should be here or have left obvious signs of their presence.

(end of discussion)

